    {
      "id": "lost_my",
      "target": "Perdí ___.",
      "pronunciation_easy": "pehr-DEE",
      "qa": "Back-translation: \"I lost ___.\" The blank takes a possessive that changes per word (mi pasaporte, mis llaves), so it is not fixed in the frame. Spain more often says \"He perdido ___\". Safety item: please verify. Word notes: wallet = \"billetera\" (\"cartera\" in Mexico and Spain, but cartera is a handbag in parts of South America); phone = \"teléfono\" (\"celular\" in Latin America, \"móvil\" in Spain); bag = \"bolsa\" (Spain: \"bolso\" for a handbag, \"mochila\" for a backpack). Room key example says \"the key to my room\"."
    },
